IMPORT prelude
IMPORT types

-- Online Safety (Minimum Age and Child Safety Risk Assessment) Bill (NZ)
-- Part 3 Subpart 2 -- Regulator-imposed enforcement measures (cll 24 to 33).
-- Source: registers/source-bundle/LMS1592864.xml, 2026 No 339-1, retrieved 2026-09-11.
--
-- Three instruments, in ascending order of intrusion: a warning (cl 24), which
-- the regulator may require the operator to republish (cl 25); an enforceable
-- undertaking (cll 27 to 30); and a corrective notice (cll 31 to 33). Two of
-- the three carry a prior-notice and hearing gate. The warning does not -- see
-- NOTES.md, incident OS-012.

§ `Part 3 Subpart 2 -- Regulator-imposed enforcement measures`

§§ `Working-day periods`

-- cl 25(3)(b) requires at least 5 working days' notice before the regulator
-- requires an operator to disclose a warning. cl 33(b) requires at least 10
-- working days before a corrective notice.

`minimum working days before a warning disclosure notice` MEANS 5
`minimum working days before a corrective notice`         MEANS 10

§§ `24. Regulator must issue warnings in certain manner, 25, 26`

DECLARE `warning` HAS
    name                                                                                IS A STRING
    -- cl 24(1)(a) and (b)
    `states the reason for the warning`                                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `is in writing and in a form approved by the regulator`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    -- cl 24(2) and (3)
    `public notice of the warning has been given`                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `personal and commercially sensitive information has been withheld`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the regulator considers publishing that information necessary or desirable`         IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Online Safety (Minimum Age and Child Safety Risk Assessment) Bill (NZ) cl 24
@export Decide whether a warning complies with clause 24
GIVEN w IS A `warning` @desc The warning: whether it states its reason, whether it is in writing in an approved form, and how personal and commercially sensitive information was treated in the public notice.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the warning complies with section 24` IF
        w's `states the reason for the warning`
    AND w's `is in writing and in a form approved by the regulator`
    AND (    w's `personal and commercially sensitive information has been withheld`
          OR w's `the regulator considers publishing that information necessary or desirable` )

DECLARE `warning disclosure notice` HAS
    name                                                                                IS A STRING
    `a warning has been issued under section 24`                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    -- cl 25(3)(a) to (c)
    `the regulator considers disclosure necessary or desirable to achieve the purpose`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `working days of written notice given before exercising the power`                   IS A NUMBER
    `the notice stated that the regulator is considering exercising the power`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice stated the reasons for considering it`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the operator was given an opportunity to make submissions and be heard`             IS A BOOLEAN
    -- cl 25(4)
    `information redacted under section 24(3) is required to be withheld`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the regulator redacted information from the publicly notified warning`              IS A BOOLEAN

-- cl 25(3)(b): the notice period is a floor, and cl 25(3)(b)(i) and (ii) fix
-- what the notice must have told the operator.
GIVEN n IS A `warning disclosure notice`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the section 25(3)(b) notice requirement is met` IF
        n's `working days of written notice given before exercising the power`
            AT LEAST `minimum working days before a warning disclosure notice`
    AND n's `the notice stated that the regulator is considering exercising the power`
    AND n's `the notice stated the reasons for considering it`

-- cl 25(4): where the regulator redacted the public warning, it must require
-- the operator to withhold the same information.
GIVEN n IS A `warning disclosure notice`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the section 25(4) redaction requirement is met` IF
    IF   n's `the regulator redacted information from the publicly notified warning`
    THEN n's `information redacted under section 24(3) is required to be withheld`
    ELSE TRUE

@ref Online Safety (Minimum Age and Child Safety Risk Assessment) Bill (NZ) cl 25
@export Decide whether the regulator may require an operator to disclose a warning
GIVEN n IS A `warning disclosure notice` @desc Whether a warning has issued, whether the regulator considers republication necessary or desirable, how many working days of notice were given and what that notice said, whether the operator was heard, and how redactions were handled.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the regulator may require the operator to disclose the warning` IF
        n's `a warning has been issued under section 24`
    AND n's `the regulator considers disclosure necessary or desirable to achieve the purpose`
    AND `the section 25(3)(b) notice requirement is met` n
    AND n's `the operator was given an opportunity to make submissions and be heard`
    AND `the section 25(4) redaction requirement is met` n

-- cl 26: failure to comply is cl 34(3)(h), a Tier 3 specified liability act.
DECLARE `notice compliance` HAS
    name                                                                                IS A STRING
    `the operator complied within the time frame specified in the notice`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the operator complied in the manner specified in the notice`                        IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Online Safety (Minimum Age and Child Safety Risk Assessment) Bill (NZ) cll 26, 32
@export Decide whether an operator has complied with a notice to disclose a warning or a corrective notice
GIVEN c IS A `notice compliance` @desc Whether the operator complied within the time frame and in the manner the notice specified.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the operator complied with the notice` IF
        c's `the operator complied within the time frame specified in the notice`
    AND c's `the operator complied in the manner specified in the notice`

§§ `27, 28, 29, 30. Enforceable undertakings`

DECLARE `undertaking` HAS
    name                                                                                IS A STRING
    -- cl 27(1)
    `is a written undertaking given by an operator in connection with enforcement`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the regulator has accepted it`                                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    -- cl 28(1)
    `the regulator gave written notice of the decision and the reasons`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    -- cl 29(1)
    `notice of acceptance has been given`                                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `a later commencement date specified by the regulator has arrived`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the regulator specified a later commencement date`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    -- cl 29(2) and (3)
    `the operator is in breach of the undertaking`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `the undertaking has been completely discharged`                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the undertaking relates to a specified liability act`                               IS A BOOLEAN

-- cl 29(1): the undertaking takes effect on the date notice of acceptance is
-- given, or at any later date the regulator specifies.
@ref Online Safety (Minimum Age and Child Safety Risk Assessment) Bill (NZ) cl 29(1)
GIVEN u IS A `undertaking`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the undertaking is in force` IF
        u's `the regulator has accepted it`
    AND u's `notice of acceptance has been given`
    AND (    NOT u's `the regulator specified a later commencement date`
          OR u's `a later commencement date specified by the regulator has arrived` )

-- cl 29(3): while the undertaking is in force and unbreached, or once completely
-- discharged, no proceedings may be brought for the act it relates to.
@ref Online Safety (Minimum Age and Child Safety Risk Assessment) Bill (NZ) cl 29(3)
@export Decide whether an undertaking bars proceedings for the specified liability act it relates to
GIVEN u IS A `undertaking` @desc The undertaking: whether it has been accepted and is in force, whether it relates to a specified liability act, whether the operator is in breach, and whether it has been completely discharged.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `proceedings are barred by the undertaking` IF
        u's `the undertaking relates to a specified liability act`
    AND (    (    `the undertaking is in force` u
              AND NOT u's `the operator is in breach of the undertaking` )
          OR u's `the undertaking has been completely discharged` )

-- cl 29(2) creates a duty not to breach an undertaking. Breach is a ground for
-- a service restriction order under cl 35(2)(c)(i)(B) and opens the cl 30 route,
-- but it is NOT one of the nine specified liability acts in cl 34(3), so no
-- pecuniary penalty is available for it. See NOTES.md, incident OS-011.

-- cl 30(2): on breach, the court may make one of two orders and no more.
DECLARE `breach of undertaking order` IS ONE OF
    `an order directing the operator to comply with the undertaking`
    `an order discharging the undertaking`

@ref Online Safety (Minimum Age and Child Safety Risk Assessment) Bill (NZ) cl 30
GIVEN u IS A `undertaking`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may make an order under section 30(2)` IF
        `the undertaking is in force` u
    AND u's `the operator is in breach of the undertaking`

§§ `31, 32, 33. Corrective notices`

DECLARE `corrective notice` HAS
    name                                                                                IS A STRING
    -- cl 31(1)(a) and (b)
    `the regulator is satisfied the operator has carried out a specified liability act`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the regulator is satisfied the operator is likely to carry out such an act`         IS A BOOLEAN
    -- cl 31(3)
    `the notice specifies a reasonable period within which the steps must be taken`      IS A BOOLEAN
    -- cl 33(a) to (c)
    `the regulator considers the notice necessary or desirable to achieve the purpose`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `working days of written notice given before exercising the power`                   IS A NUMBER
    `the notice stated that the regulator is considering exercising the power`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the notice stated the reasons for considering it`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the operator was given an opportunity to make submissions and be heard`             IS A BOOLEAN

-- cl 31(1): the trigger is satisfaction as to a past or a likely future act.
GIVEN c IS A `corrective notice`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the section 31(1) trigger is met` IF
        c's `the regulator is satisfied the operator has carried out a specified liability act`
    OR  c's `the regulator is satisfied the operator is likely to carry out such an act`

-- cl 33: the same three-limb gate as cl 25(3), with a 10 working day floor.
GIVEN c IS A `corrective notice`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the section 33 procedural gate is met` IF
        c's `the regulator considers the notice necessary or desirable to achieve the purpose`
    AND c's `working days of written notice given before exercising the power`
            AT LEAST `minimum working days before a corrective notice`
    AND c's `the notice stated that the regulator is considering exercising the power`
    AND c's `the notice stated the reasons for considering it`
    AND c's `the operator was given an opportunity to make submissions and be heard`

@ref Online Safety (Minimum Age and Child Safety Risk Assessment) Bill (NZ) cll 31, 33
@export Decide whether the regulator may issue a corrective notice
GIVEN c IS A `corrective notice` @desc Whether the regulator is satisfied as to a past or likely specified liability act, whether the notice specifies a reasonable period for the steps, and whether the cl 33 notice-and-hearing gate is satisfied.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the regulator may issue a corrective notice` IF
        `the section 31(1) trigger is met` c
    AND c's `the notice specifies a reasonable period within which the steps must be taken`
    AND `the section 33 procedural gate is met` c

§§ `Scenario fixtures`

`a corrective notice on short notice` MEANS `corrective notice` WITH
    name                                                                                IS "seven working days' notice"
    `the regulator is satisfied the operator has carried out a specified liability act`  IS TRUE
    `the regulator is satisfied the operator is likely to carry out such an act`         IS FALSE
    `the notice specifies a reasonable period within which the steps must be taken`      IS TRUE
    `the regulator considers the notice necessary or desirable to achieve the purpose`   IS TRUE
    `working days of written notice given before exercising the power`                   IS 7
    `the notice stated that the regulator is considering exercising the power`           IS TRUE
    `the notice stated the reasons for considering it`                                   IS TRUE
    `the operator was given an opportunity to make submissions and be heard`             IS TRUE

`a corrective notice properly given` MEANS `corrective notice` WITH
    name                                                                                IS "ten working days' notice, anticipated act"
    `the regulator is satisfied the operator has carried out a specified liability act`  IS FALSE
    `the regulator is satisfied the operator is likely to carry out such an act`         IS TRUE
    `the notice specifies a reasonable period within which the steps must be taken`      IS TRUE
    `the regulator considers the notice necessary or desirable to achieve the purpose`   IS TRUE
    `working days of written notice given before exercising the power`                   IS 10
    `the notice stated that the regulator is considering exercising the power`           IS TRUE
    `the notice stated the reasons for considering it`                                   IS TRUE
    `the operator was given an opportunity to make submissions and be heard`             IS TRUE

`an undertaking in force and kept` MEANS `undertaking` WITH
    name                                                                                IS "remediation undertaking, on foot"
    `is a written undertaking given by an operator in connection with enforcement`       IS TRUE
    `the regulator has accepted it`                                                      IS TRUE
    `the regulator gave written notice of the decision and the reasons`                  IS TRUE
    `notice of acceptance has been given`                                                IS TRUE
    `a later commencement date specified by the regulator has arrived`                   IS FALSE
    `the regulator specified a later commencement date`                                  IS FALSE
    `the operator is in breach of the undertaking`                                       IS FALSE
    `the undertaking has been completely discharged`                                     IS FALSE
    `the undertaking relates to a specified liability act`                               IS TRUE

`an undertaking in breach` MEANS `undertaking` WITH
    name                                                                                IS "remediation undertaking, breached"
    `is a written undertaking given by an operator in connection with enforcement`       IS TRUE
    `the regulator has accepted it`                                                      IS TRUE
    `the regulator gave written notice of the decision and the reasons`                  IS TRUE
    `notice of acceptance has been given`                                                IS TRUE
    `a later commencement date specified by the regulator has arrived`                   IS FALSE
    `the regulator specified a later commencement date`                                  IS FALSE
    `the operator is in breach of the undertaking`                                       IS TRUE
    `the undertaking has been completely discharged`                                     IS FALSE
    `the undertaking relates to a specified liability act`                               IS TRUE

§§ `Machine-evaluated cases`

-- cl 33(b): the 10 working day floor is a precondition, so a notice given on
-- seven working days is outside the power however sound its merits.
#EVAL `the regulator may issue a corrective notice` `a corrective notice on short notice`
#ASSERT `the section 33 procedural gate is met` `a corrective notice on short notice` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the regulator may issue a corrective notice` `a corrective notice on short notice` EQUALS FALSE

-- cl 31(1)(b): satisfaction that an act is LIKELY is enough; no past act is needed.
#ASSERT `the regulator may issue a corrective notice` `a corrective notice properly given` EQUALS TRUE

-- cl 29(3)(a): while the undertaking is in force and unbreached, proceedings for
-- the act it relates to are barred. Once breached, the bar lifts.
#EVAL `proceedings are barred by the undertaking` `an undertaking in force and kept`
#EVAL `proceedings are barred by the undertaking` `an undertaking in breach`
#ASSERT `proceedings are barred by the undertaking` `an undertaking in force and kept` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `proceedings are barred by the undertaking` `an undertaking in breach` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the court may make an order under section 30(2)` `an undertaking in breach` EQUALS TRUE
